{title: Jesus Is All the World to Me}
{artist: Will L. Thompson}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Jesus is all the world to me, my [A7]life, my joy, my [D]all
He is my strength from day to day, with[G]out Him [A7]I would [D]fall
When I am sad, to Him I go, no [A7]other one can cheer me [D]so
When I am sad, He makes me [G]glad, [A7]He's my [D]Friend
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Jesus is all the world to me, my [A7]Friend in trials [D]sore
I go to Him for blessings, and [G]He gives [A7]them o'er and [D]o'er
He sends the sunshine and the rain, He [A7]sends the harvest's golden [D]grain
Sunshine and rain, harvest of [G]grain, [A7]He's my [D]Friend
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Jesus is all the world to me, and [A7]true to Him I'll [D]be
O how could I this Friend de[G]ny, when [A7]He's so true to [D]me
Following Him I know I'm right, He [A7]watches o'er me day and [D]night
Following Him by day and [G]night, [A7]He's my [D]Friend
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Jesus is all the world to me, I [A7]want no better [D]Friend
I trust Him now, I'll [G]trust Him [A7]when life's fleeting days shall [D]end
Beautiful life with such a Friend, [A7]beautiful life that has no [D]end
Eternal life, eternal [G]joy, [A7]He's my [D]Friend
{end_of_verse}
